1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:13,972
[Ivy] <i>Raul tipped him off</i>
<i>that the Ardientes know</i>

3
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:15,473
<i>where the safe house is.</i>

4
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:16,891
[Jepoy] <i>I'll handle that, Ivy.</i>
<i>I'll find out.</i>

5
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:19,811
[Raul] <i>What's important is</i>
<i>she's ready for the Ardientes.</i>

6
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:21,730
<i>Dad, you might get in trouble for this.</i>

7
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:25,066
<i>I can help Camia more</i>
<i>if I stay here with the Ardientes.</i>

8
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,192
[Emilia] <i>You traitor!</i>

9
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:28,528
<i>I will find out who you're working with!</i>

10
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:30,238
[Arnaldo] <i>If you still want to</i>
<i>see your daughter alive,</i>

11
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:31,364
<i>you'll come see me.</i>

12
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:32,866
[Tonio] <i>Have you seen Esther</i>
<i>and Edward around?</i>

13
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:34,534
<i>We've been looking for them all day.</i>

14
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,494
[Camia] <i>Esther and Edward are in danger.</i>

15
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:39,164
<i>Not just them, but all our witnesses.</i>

16
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:41,583
[Noel] <i>What's going on?</i>
<i>Have the Ardientes found us?</i>

17
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:43,877
[Tonio] <i>I bet Edward and Esther</i>
<i>ratted us out.</i>

18
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,129
[Arnaldo] <i>Break down the door!</i>
<i>Leave no one alive!</i>

19
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:47,672
[gunshots]

20
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:49,674
[Gino] <i>Let's focus on the issue here.</i>

21
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:52,051
<i>Camia Cruz. Is what she's saying true?</i>

22
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,970
<i>These are all false allegations.</i>

23
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:55,263
<i>Think about it.</i>

24
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:58,183
<i>What father could ever kill</i>
<i>his own children?</i>

25
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:00,560
<i>And to my children in Ardiente,</i>
<i>you know the truth.</i>

26
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:03,063
<i>Your Señor Julio loves you.</i>

27
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:06,107
-<i>Ivy, they're not there.</i>
-[Ivy] <i>We have to secure Tonio.</i>

28
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>Tonio escaped, Grandpa.</i>
<i>We don't know who helped him.</i>

29
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:11,488
[Julio] <i>Clean up your mother's mess.</i>

30
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:13,281
[Camia] <i>Your men called me.</i>

31
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>Lily, they're all dead.</i>

32
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:16,493
[screams]

33
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:19,329
[Ivy] <i>After everything we've done!</i>

34
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:22,040
<i>Mayor. Everything you want</i>
<i>to know about Tonio</i>

35
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,708
<i>and his family is in here.</i>

36
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:26,211
[Georgina] <i>The prosecution</i>
<i>calls Mr. Antonio Vidal</i>

37
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:27,337
<i>to the witness stand.</i>

38
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:33,218
<i>Did former governor Emilia Torillo</i>
<i>order you to rape and kill Camia Cruz?</i>

39
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:34,260
[Tonio] <i>No, your Honor.</i>

40
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:37,305
[tense music playing]

41
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:41,017
Let me remind you, Mr. Vidal.

42
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:44,729
You released a statement
saying Mrs. Torillo ordered you.

43
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:49,609
Are you telling us you lied?

44
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:59,911
Yes, your Honor. I lied.
I'm taking back my statement.

45
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:04,124
[Georgina] Lying under oath
is a very serious offense, Mr. Vidal.

46
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,543
You can go to jail.

47
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:10,255
I'm sorry.

48
00:02:11,464 --> 00:02:15,552
Did someone order you
to change your testimony?

49
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:18,346
Did someone threaten your life?

50
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:20,431
[tense music playing]

51
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:32,110
No one did. This was my own decision.

52
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:37,490
I just wanted to extort money
from the Ardientes…

53
00:02:40,076 --> 00:02:41,786
but I feel guilty now.

54
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:49,502
I'm retracting my first statement.

55
00:02:50,753 --> 00:02:53,798
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

56
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:05,768
[tense music playing]

57
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,992
[action music playing]

58
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:38,801
"Hi, baby!"

59
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:41,304
<i>Ma'am, I'll go out for a while.</i>

60
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:42,388
[Tonio's wife] <i>Okay.</i>

61
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:46,976
<i>Sweetie, finish that up so we can sleep.</i>

62
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,061
<i>Okay.</i>

63
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:50,521
[beeping sound]

64
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:53,107
[tense music playing]

65
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:56,110
"It's Daddy. I miss you!"

66
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:57,195
[Rosalie] <i>What?</i>

67
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,948
<i>Why did Daddy make a new account?</i>

68
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:08,665
[beeping sound]

69
00:04:08,998 --> 00:04:09,958
[Rosalie] IS THIS A NEW ACCOUNT?

70
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,417
[Arnaldo] THIS IS MY SECRET
ACCOUNT. DON'T TELL ANYONE.

71
00:04:15,838 --> 00:04:17,006
[Arnaldo] I WANNA SEE YOU.

72
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:18,132
WHERE ARE YOU? PLEASE!

73
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:23,096
<i>Hello? Baby? Hey.</i>

74
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:24,889
[Tonio] <i>Why did you call?</i>

75
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,433
[Tonio's wife] <i>I'm begging you!</i>

76
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:30,979
<i>Please let us go!</i>
<i>We've done nothing wrong!</i>

77
00:04:31,062 --> 00:04:33,273
<i>Daddy T. Where are you?</i>

78
00:04:33,356 --> 00:04:34,607
<i>I miss you so much.</i>

79
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:37,860
<i>Who are you?</i>

80
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:39,362
<i>Didn't I tell you I'd find you?</i>

81
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:43,157
<i>Where's my daughter? Where's my family?</i>

82
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:45,243
<i>You want to talk</i>
<i>to your daughter? Here she is.</i>

83
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,495
<i>-Daddy!</i>
<i>-Tonio!</i>

84
00:04:47,578 --> 00:04:48,579
<i>-Help us!</i>
<i>-Rosalie!</i>

85
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:49,414
<i>…Daddy!</i>

86
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:50,331
<i>-Tonio…</i>
<i>-Rosalie!</i>

87
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,374
[Tonio's wife] <i>I'm begging you!</i>

88
00:04:51,457 --> 00:04:54,585
<i>-Help me!</i>
<i>-So… Are we good?</i>

89
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:56,212
<i>Is that okay? Now…</i>

90
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:58,089
<i>if you still want them to live,</i>

91
00:04:58,423 --> 00:05:00,049
<i>you'll do exactly as I say.</i>

92
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:01,676
<i>Do you understand?</i>

93
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:03,594
<i>Okay.</i>

94
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,306
<i>Okay.</i>

95
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:07,807
<i>I'll do anything you want.</i>

96
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,684
<i>Just please don't hurt my family.</i>

97
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,227
<i>That's what I wanted to hear.</i>

98
00:05:12,937 --> 00:05:14,314
<i>Tonio!</i>

99
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:22,447
No one told me to do this.

100
00:05:23,072 --> 00:05:27,201
I'm just telling the truth,
so I can clear my conscience.

101
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:29,746
[ominous music playing]

102
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:35,960
Governor Torillo never ordered
me to rape and kill Camia Cruz.

103
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:44,802
The Ardientes never ordered me
to kill anyone.

104
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:53,144
[Emilia] Ivy!

105
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:57,523
[Emilia] I'm so happy the truth
is finally out.

106
00:05:57,815 --> 00:05:59,734
-Yes, congratulations, Emilia.
-I know!

107
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:01,194
Thank you! Thank you.

108
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:03,863
Papa.

109
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:10,536
[sinister music playing]

110
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:22,256
The Ardientes would've killed my family…

111
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:25,093
if I didn't retract my statement.

112
00:06:25,676 --> 00:06:28,137
But I didn't rat you out, Miss Ivy.

113
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:30,598
I owe so much to you.

114
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:32,809
I already owe you my life.

115
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,561
I didn't mean for this to happen.

116
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:37,897
Please forgive me.

117
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:39,816
Diego…

118
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:42,652
Did you say anything to your father?

119
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:47,365
No. Believe me, I wouldn't do that.

120
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:49,575
[tense music playing]

121
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:50,660
I know.

122
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,413
[Carlotta] But how did this happen?

123
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:07,426
You did it, Arnaldo.
Not that I had any doubts.

124
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:12,640
But you've secured a victory
for us in this legal battle.

125
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:14,016
Of course, Grandpa.

126
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:18,229
Like you said. Failure is not an option.

127
00:07:19,063 --> 00:07:20,189
[scoffs]

128
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:22,400
Here's to you.

129
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:28,781
[sinister music playing]

130
00:07:36,914 --> 00:07:39,542
[soft music playing]

131
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:55,933
This isn't over, Mom.

132
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:00,605
Whatever happens in court…

133
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:05,026
win or lose, this isn't over.

134
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:09,614
I will continue to fight.

135
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:17,121
[somber music playing]

136
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:36,516
Due to insufficient testimonies
and evidence submitted in court,

137
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:40,353
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo and Raul Torillo…

138
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:45,358
are hereby declared innocent of the rape,

139
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:48,861
abduction, and illegal imprisonment
of Camia Cruz.

140
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:50,821
[Ardiente allies applauding]

141
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:54,951
[gavel banging]

142
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:58,037
[woman] Wonderful news.

143
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:05,127
[tense music playing]

144
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:46,752
[tense music playing]

145
00:09:56,512 --> 00:10:00,391
Gentlemen…
to the victor belong the spoils!

146
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:03,936
-Cheers!
-Congratulations!

147
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:07,148
Congratulations, Papa!
You dodged that bullet.

148
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:09,775
Right. You know, Emilia…

149
00:10:11,068 --> 00:10:15,114
I never once felt worried
about the lawsuit.

150
00:10:15,906 --> 00:10:22,038
Because I knew that my favorite
grandson would find a way.

151
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:27,001
[emphatic] Arnaldo, you are the man!

152
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:29,378
If not for you…

153
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:32,715
your parents would've been imprisoned now…

154
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:37,678
and all of us Ardientes would
have lost our reputation.

155
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:40,640
I told you I'd find
that bastard, didn't I?

156
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:45,019
This is your best work yet, my grandson.

157
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,605
I'm very proud of you.

158
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:51,567
Thank you. Who else would I take after?

159
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:52,652
I learned from the best.

160
00:10:53,944 --> 00:10:56,864
-Well… Cheers!
-[all] Cheers!

161
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:58,824
-To Mayor Arnaldo!
-Cheers!

162
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:01,369
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

163
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:10,252
-Daddy!
-[ecstatic] Rosalie!

164
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:24,392
As agreed, I have your family with me.

165
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:28,813
All of your passports are here.

166
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:31,565
You'll be in Thailand tomorrow morning.

167
00:11:31,649 --> 00:11:32,942
Everything you need to know

168
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:34,276
about the trip is in that envelope.

169
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,195
Thank you, Miss Ivy.

170
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:38,823
[tense music playing]

171
00:11:45,496 --> 00:11:46,956
Unlike you, Tonio,

172
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,751
I'm always true to my word.

173
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:53,421
[tense music playing]

174
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:13,357
It's going to be tough
to bring down the Ardientes.

175
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:16,986
We need help from the opposition.

176
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:18,988
What about Senator Magno?

177
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:23,534
Nanny, we need to be more careful.

178
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:28,080
They have their own personal
and political agendas.

179
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:31,375
We can't just trust them so easily.

180
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,294
[Jepoy] Leave that to me, Ivy.

181
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:35,713
I'll get all Senator Magno's papers

182
00:12:35,796 --> 00:12:38,174
at the Ardientes' mansion.
We're running out of time.

183
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:41,093
I'll also get the camera
I hid in Julio's room.

184
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:43,929
I'm sure we can get some evidence from it.

185
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:46,557
Jepoy.

186
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:49,226
You need to be careful.

187
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:52,480
The Ardientes are more cautious now.

188
00:12:52,563 --> 00:12:55,107
Don't make a move
unless you're sure about it.

189
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:56,358
[phone ringing]

190
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:58,986
[line ringing]

191
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:00,988
Diego?

192
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:04,033
-Ivy, it's about to start.
-Thank you.

193
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,534
Nanny, the TV.

194
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:07,077
[sinister music playing]

195
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:08,370
[reporter] Miss Camia's here.

196
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,080
Miss Camia, any comments?

197
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:13,667
[indistinct chatter on TV]

198
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:15,503
[reporter] What's your message
for the Ardientes?

199
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,462
[indistinct chatter]

200
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:17,755
[reporter] What's your next move?

201
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:19,965
Is it true that you had an affair
with Mr. Raul Torillo?

202
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:23,719
We all know why the case
against the Ardientes

203
00:13:23,802 --> 00:13:25,387
was dismissed.

204
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:31,060
Because they threatened
and had the witnesses killed

205
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:34,146
so no one could prove
the crimes they committed.

206
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:37,691
[Camia] <i>Well… I'm not afraid of them.</i>

207
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:39,318
[sinister music playing]

208
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,321
<i>And they can't stop me</i>
<i>from seeking justice</i>

209
00:13:42,404 --> 00:13:44,698
<i>for what they did to me.</i>

210
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:47,034
<i>For killing my husband</i>

211
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:49,662
<i>and hundreds of other innocent people.</i>

212
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:53,958
I may have lost this battle,
but I will win the war.

213
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:56,585
[Camia] <i>It's just the beginning.</i>

214
00:13:57,795 --> 00:14:03,092
<i>And I won't stop until I expose</i>
<i>all the Ardientes dirty secrets!</i>

215
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,845
-[man] Viva Ardiente!
-[woman] Viva Ardiente!

216
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:07,930
-Mom.
-<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

217
00:14:08,013 --> 00:14:10,516
-[Diego] Miss Camia, let's go.
-[all] Viva Ardiente!

218
00:14:10,599 --> 00:14:13,769
-[woman] <i>You're despicable!</i>
-[man] We won the case!

219
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:16,939
[reporter] <i>Any message</i>
<i>to the supporters of Ardientes?</i>

220
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:19,483
[Ardientes' supporters]
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

221
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:21,569
[sinister music playing]

222
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:34,832
[Ivy] Mom! Mom!

223
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:36,584
Ivy.

224
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:39,670
Mom, are you all right? Are you hurt?

225
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:40,963
How about you, Diego?

226
00:14:41,046 --> 00:14:42,506
We're both fine now.

227
00:14:43,048 --> 00:14:45,259
The one who threw a rock
at Mrs. Camia was apprehended.

228
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:46,552
An Ardiente loyalist.

229
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:51,181
I better tighten the security, then.

230
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:52,975
You don't have to.

231
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:55,978
What matters is Diego and I are safe.

232
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:59,648
No, I have to do it.
Espiritu, I want guard dogs.

233
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:03,068
I want you to set checkpoints up
at every corner. Is that clear?

234
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:04,695
-Yes, ma'am.
-Do it right now!

235
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:08,574
As I said, Mom,
your safety is my top priority.

236
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:11,869
I'm glad you're okay.

237
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:17,958
Diego, thank you.

238
00:15:20,502 --> 00:15:23,505
[Julio] What do you mean, Arnaldo?

239
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:28,677
Tonio was able to leave
the country without us knowing?

240
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:31,805
Grandpa, I had Tonio and
his family closely monitored.

241
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:35,225
But someone helped them.
So, they managed to escape.

242
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:37,603
The question is, who?

243
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:40,105
Camia doesn't have
the resources to do that.

244
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:41,941
Well, whoever it was,

245
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:44,234
they're obviously
powerful enough to do it.

246
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:47,863
I'm suspecting Senator Magno,
but we're not sure yet.

247
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:51,951
How can we make sure Tonio
will keep quiet?

248
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:54,495
-That he won't appear again?
-I doubt it.

249
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:57,957
After I threatened Tonio and his family…

250
00:15:58,540 --> 00:15:59,667
I'm sure he'll keep his mouth shut.

251
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,002
One more slip-up, and I'll wipe them out.

252
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:04,213
Just like how I took care
of all the other witnesses.

253
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:06,715
Good. As for me,

254
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:09,969
I'll silence Camia once and
for all to solve our problem.

255
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:11,887
Slow down, Emilia.

256
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:14,932
We managed to remain Scot-free

257
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:16,558
after having those witnesses killed.

258
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:18,519
But Camia Cruz…

259
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:22,690
She's too high a risk to take right now.

260
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,484
And the media has its eyes on us.

261
00:16:26,568 --> 00:16:30,948
As long as that's the case,
we can't touch Camia Cruz.

262
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,201
For now, what we should do…

263
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:39,206
is make sure they won't get
any more witnesses to help them.

264
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:46,171
And, Emilia… You better watch Raul.

265
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:49,842
He's crazy over Camia Cruz.

266
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:54,304
Make sure he isn't betraying us.

267
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,099
Yes, Papa.

268
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:05,607
I'm sorry, but you can't come here.

269
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:07,901
I just want to talk to Camia.

270
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:09,695
I'm sorry, but you can't do that.

271
00:17:09,778 --> 00:17:11,822
-I just want to talk to her!
-Sir.

272
00:17:11,905 --> 00:17:13,157
-Stop, sir.
-Camia! Camia!

273
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:14,199
-Camia!
-You have to…

274
00:17:14,283 --> 00:17:15,784
-to leave, sir.
-Camia! Come out now!

275
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:16,618
Camia! Wait!

276
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:17,745
-You have to leave, sir.
-Ouch!

277
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:21,790
Wait! Ouch! Hey! Camia! Camia!

278
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:25,044
-Camia! Hey!
-You can't go here, sir.

279
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:26,795
Who is that? What's going on?

280
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,547
Ma'am, someone's causing a scene outside.

281
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:30,382
-Who?
-It's Raul Torillo.

282
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:32,301
You know what to do.

283
00:17:32,384 --> 00:17:33,844
Don't you ever let him set foot in here.

284
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:34,928
Yes, ma'am.

285
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:36,805
[tense music playing]

286
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:38,599
Raul isn't in his room.

287
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:41,143
But don't worry. I had someone follow him.

288
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:43,103
[tense music playing]

289
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:47,566
I just want to talk to you!
Wait. Wait. Camia!

290
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:49,568
-Sir, please.
-Camia, please talk to me!

291
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:50,903
I want to know if you're safe!

292
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:52,237
Last warning, sir. Leave.

293
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:54,448
You know how much I love you! Camia!

294
00:17:54,531 --> 00:17:56,575
[dog barking]

295
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:59,078
Last warning, sir. You should leave now.

296
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:01,789
[dog barking]

297
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:05,751
[tense music playing]

298
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:17,471
[phone dings]

299
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:20,432
[Raul] <i>Camia, you know</i>
<i>how much I love you!</i>

300
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:21,475
<i>Camia, talk to me!</i>

301
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:22,768
[guard] <i>Sir, you have to leave.</i>

302
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:24,728
[Raul] <i>Camia!</i>

303
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:25,813
[scoffs]

304
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,606
So you love her?

305
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,161
[tense music playing]

306
00:18:54,174 --> 00:18:55,175
[nervously exhales]

307
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:06,812
[door opening]

308
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:12,192
[sinister music playing]

309
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:14,278
Madrigal.

310
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:19,533
What are you doing in my office?

311
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:24,496
Congressman, the nurse asked me
to bring your medicine here.

312
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:27,916
I'm sorry.

313
00:19:32,045 --> 00:19:33,380
All right. You may leave now.

314
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:35,883
[sinister music playing]

315
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:02,618
[sinister music playing]

316
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:16,423
[line ringing]

317
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:20,302
Hello, Arnaldo.

318
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:25,849
Keep an eye on Madrigal.

319
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:33,607
[somber music playing]

320
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:44,993
Why are you awake? Why aren't you in bed?

321
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:48,205
Well, I'm just having
a few drinks. Care to join me?

322
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:50,874
No, thanks. Well then…

323
00:20:52,459 --> 00:20:53,502
Where've you been?

324
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:55,712
[tense music playing]

325
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:00,509
I was with some of my business partners.

326
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:03,845
We talked about some new plans.

327
00:21:05,722 --> 00:21:06,723
Good night.

328
00:21:10,769 --> 00:21:12,354
Such a terrible liar.

329
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:18,443
[phone ringing]

330
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:20,696
Lily, what's wrong?

331
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:22,739
Mom, I'm in the car behind you.

332
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:24,741
<i>Do you really need to come here?</i>

333
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:28,704
Lily, why did you follow me?
Someone might see you.

334
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,872
-Mom.
-<i>Lily, dear.</i>

335
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:32,749
Our supporters organized…

336
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:34,126
<i>this event.</i>

337
00:21:34,459 --> 00:21:35,961
They're victims of the Ardientes too.

338
00:21:36,044 --> 00:21:37,546
I want to support them.

339
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:39,673
Mom, I understand that.

340
00:21:39,798 --> 00:21:42,801
But every time you leave the house…

341
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:45,345
I can't help but worry about you.

342
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:47,848
Lily, I can't just sit there all the time.

343
00:21:48,598 --> 00:21:49,975
<i>We're in this together,</i>

344
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:51,727
<i>regardless of the danger we're facing.</i>

345
00:21:51,852 --> 00:21:53,270
Even if you surround me

346
00:21:53,353 --> 00:21:56,898
with a hundred bodyguards,
we can't always be safe.

347
00:21:57,357 --> 00:21:58,650
<i>But we shouldn't be afraid</i>

348
00:21:58,734 --> 00:22:01,403
because if we are, we'll lose the fight.

349
00:22:03,155 --> 00:22:04,197
Okay, Mom.

350
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,491
Don't worry. I'll be with Diego.

351
00:22:06,908 --> 00:22:08,660
-Okay.
-Okay, bye.

352
00:22:12,581 --> 00:22:14,249
[ominous music playing]

353
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:19,713
Let's go.

354
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:30,265
[action music playing]

355
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:38,023
Mrs. Camia, no one's here yet.

356
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:44,154
[goon] Freeze! Nobody move!

357
00:22:44,362 --> 00:22:46,198
Nobody move! Hands up!

358
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:47,491
[goon] Hands up!

359
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:50,494
Let go of me!

360
00:22:51,078 --> 00:22:52,079
[thud]

361
00:22:52,913 --> 00:22:53,955
Stop it!

362
00:22:54,623 --> 00:22:56,374
Who sent you here?

363
00:22:57,834 --> 00:22:59,002
Stop the car!

364
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:02,798
Emilia…

365
00:23:04,257 --> 00:23:05,759
[tense music playing]

366
00:23:20,148 --> 00:23:22,150
[foreboding music playing]

367
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:26,780
[door closes]

368
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:34,037
Hi, my dear Camia! Camia, Camia, darling!

369
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:36,623
[Emilia sighs]

370
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:38,750
Let go of her.

371
00:23:40,335 --> 00:23:41,461
Look at you.

372
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:44,297
You're so beautiful.

373
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,884
And you smell nice!

374
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:49,386
[laughs]

375
00:23:50,971 --> 00:23:52,097
Oh, Diego.

376
00:23:53,056 --> 00:23:55,475
No wonder my husband is crazy about you.

377
00:23:55,809 --> 00:23:58,395
You're like an angel sent from heaven!

378
00:23:58,478 --> 00:24:01,189
Not once in my life have I ever
been interested in your husband.

379
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:04,359
I'm never going to steal him from you!

380
00:24:04,568 --> 00:24:08,029
He's all yours!
Stick it in that brain of yours!

381
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:11,283
Wow! Thanks, darling!
That's very comforting!

382
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:17,539
But we still have a problem.
Because whatever I do to Raul…

383
00:24:18,957 --> 00:24:20,792
my husband is addicted to you.

384
00:24:21,751 --> 00:24:24,754
-That's your problem!
-It's my problem, your problem,

385
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:27,424
my husband's problem,
it's everyone's problem!

386
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:32,596
You know, my efforts to hurt Raul
have no effect on him.

387
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:35,807
But what if I hurt you?

388
00:24:36,683 --> 00:24:38,435
Will he come to his senses?

389
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:40,770
Do whatever you want to do.

390
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:44,941
You had me raped once,
and you had me buried alive.

391
00:24:45,025 --> 00:24:47,110
There's nothing else
I have to fear from you!

392
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:51,698
[teasing] Wow! Bravo, bravo!

393
00:24:51,781 --> 00:24:54,826
You're so brave! That's what I love!

394
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:59,539
And true, you've faced
death before, right?

395
00:24:59,623 --> 00:25:01,458
Whoops. Almost.

396
00:25:02,417 --> 00:25:07,380
What if this time, I bring you closer?

397
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:12,010
Close? She's standing right
in front of me now!

398
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:13,303
Hmm?

399
00:25:13,386 --> 00:25:15,222
Closer? This is close!

400
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:17,599
Let go of me!

401
00:25:19,601 --> 00:25:21,978
Do you want more? More?! More?!

402
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:23,813
[Camia laughs]

403
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:26,066
You know, Emilia, you're so funny.

404
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:31,321
Because no matter what you do,

405
00:25:32,405 --> 00:25:34,658
your husband doesn't respect you.

406
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:37,661
And I know that
even if you have me killed now,

407
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:40,330
your husband will never love you!

408
00:25:40,413 --> 00:25:41,790
So you really want more?!

409
00:25:44,125 --> 00:25:44,918
You monster!

410
00:25:45,001 --> 00:25:47,212
Murderer! Murderer!

411
00:25:47,295 --> 00:25:48,672
-[Ivy] Emilia!
-[Diego] Mrs. Camia, stop!

412
00:25:48,755 --> 00:25:50,131
Let go of me! Hey!

413
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:53,093
That's enough! Emilia, that's enough!

414
00:25:53,176 --> 00:25:54,010
Ouch.

415
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:57,180
What on earth are you doing?!
You're causing another scandal!

416
00:25:57,764 --> 00:26:00,016
What will your father,
the Congressman, say?

417
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:01,643
What will the people of Ardiente say?

418
00:26:01,726 --> 00:26:03,103
You're at it again.

419
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:06,564
You just had your lawsuit dismissed.

420
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:10,652
What else do you want? A reunion in court?

421
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:12,862
[tense music playing]

422
00:26:12,946 --> 00:26:14,906
And what the hell are you doing here?

423
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:16,116
[suspenseful sting]

424
00:26:21,746 --> 00:26:23,373
[tense music playing]

425
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,296
I saw you on the way here.

426
00:26:29,587 --> 00:26:31,423
And I wanted to come in and say hi.

427
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:36,136
And… wow, Emilia. I sure was surprised.

428
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:37,721
[sighs]

429
00:26:43,351 --> 00:26:44,436
What's with that look?

430
00:26:47,355 --> 00:26:48,940
Are you actually suspecting me?

431
00:26:53,236 --> 00:26:55,822
I couldn't care less about this woman.

432
00:26:59,784 --> 00:27:03,204
But, you… Aren't we friends?

433
00:27:04,164 --> 00:27:06,082
I'm just concerned about you, Emilia.

434
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:16,843
Oops. I'm sorry again.

435
00:27:17,719 --> 00:27:19,054
[laughing]

436
00:27:21,181 --> 00:27:22,849
[tense music playing]

437
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:38,281
Mom.

438
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:41,034
Mom.

439
00:27:41,826 --> 00:27:43,328
How many times do I have to tell you

440
00:27:43,411 --> 00:27:44,746
that I can take care of myself?

441
00:27:48,833 --> 00:27:49,834
Mom…

442
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:53,338
You can't stop me from worrying.

443
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:56,716
From worrying that I'll lose you again.

444
00:27:58,009 --> 00:28:00,804
Mom, I was just a kid when
they first took you from me.

445
00:28:00,929 --> 00:28:03,807
I couldn't do anything.
But it's different now.

446
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:07,352
So I can't stop myself from protecting you

447
00:28:07,435 --> 00:28:10,438
when they're hurting you
right in front of me!

448
00:28:10,688 --> 00:28:12,774
But I won't allow you

449
00:28:12,857 --> 00:28:16,069
to get hurt in exchange for protecting me.

450
00:28:16,277 --> 00:28:18,321
-[frustrated] Mom…
-Lily, listen…

451
00:28:20,657 --> 00:28:23,118
I know the danger I'm in.

452
00:28:24,577 --> 00:28:27,580
And you're not the only one who's worried

453
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:31,042
that the Ardientes
will tear us apart again.

454
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:34,504
I know you're putting yourself
in grave danger

455
00:28:34,796 --> 00:28:36,840
just so can we obtain justice.

456
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:42,804
But, Lily, don't give them
any reasons to suspect you.

457
00:28:50,854 --> 00:28:52,480
[tense music playing]

458
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:54,774
-[heavy footsteps]
-[grunts]

459
00:28:55,358 --> 00:28:56,359
[sighs]

460
00:28:58,111 --> 00:28:59,487
[heavy breathing]

461
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:04,784
-What happened, Emilia?
-Auntie, where's Raul?

462
00:29:05,201 --> 00:29:06,077
In his room.

463
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:09,998
Can you please tell me what happened?

464
00:29:10,081 --> 00:29:11,958
I confronted that Camia woman, Auntie.

465
00:29:12,542 --> 00:29:15,211
-[confused] What?!
-Yes, Auntie. I confronted her.

466
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:18,465
And I told her to keep her paws
off my husband.

467
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:21,926
But, someone got in my way.
Guess who? Ivy.

468
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:25,138
She just came out of nowhere
and pulled me.

469
00:29:25,555 --> 00:29:27,056
And why would she do that?

470
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:30,810
Exactly. I don't know, either.

471
00:29:30,935 --> 00:29:34,105
But, I have a feeling
she did it to protect Camia.

472
00:29:34,564 --> 00:29:38,276
You know what? I smell a traitor
in our own backyard.

473
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:41,863
Are you telling me that Ivy
and Camia are working together?

474
00:29:42,113 --> 00:29:43,448
Nothing's impossible, Auntie.

475
00:29:43,656 --> 00:29:46,242
That's why I need to find out
how they're connected.

476
00:29:55,543 --> 00:29:57,504
[Carlotta] How's your mother, Ivy?

477
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:00,757
She's fine now, Nanny Carlotta.

478
00:30:00,965 --> 00:30:02,884
But, this should never happen again.

479
00:30:03,843 --> 00:30:05,220
And what about you?

480
00:30:07,096 --> 00:30:08,348
I'll be fine.

481
00:30:09,432 --> 00:30:11,810
I just have to be careful now.

482
00:30:12,268 --> 00:30:15,188
I get reckless
whenever my mother's involved.

483
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:17,732
All right. I'll get you
something to eat, okay?

484
00:30:19,609 --> 00:30:23,238
Ivy. I'm sorry, I failed
to watch over Emilia.

485
00:30:23,863 --> 00:30:25,532
Jepoy, it's not your fault.

486
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:26,991
Ivy, you don't understand.

487
00:30:27,784 --> 00:30:28,701
It is my fault.

488
00:30:28,785 --> 00:30:30,495
You don't know how much
I worried about you.

489
00:30:30,578 --> 00:30:32,330
[soft music playing]

490
00:30:32,413 --> 00:30:34,207
For sure, Emilia's suspecting you now.

491
00:30:34,290 --> 00:30:35,333
I need to do something.

492
00:30:37,544 --> 00:30:40,964
Just make sure you won't
get yourself in danger, Jepoy.

493
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:44,300
You've done so much for me.

494
00:30:44,801 --> 00:30:46,719
Even things you shouldn't have done.

495
00:30:46,886 --> 00:30:47,804
That's not enough, Ivy.

496
00:30:48,179 --> 00:30:50,056
How's it not enough, Jepoy?

497
00:30:50,557 --> 00:30:53,726
You're risking your life
every day just for me.

498
00:30:53,935 --> 00:30:56,229
Just to help me with my plans.

499
00:30:56,312 --> 00:30:57,313
Ivy, you don't understand.

500
00:30:57,397 --> 00:30:58,982
That's not enough because I love you.

501
00:30:59,315 --> 00:31:02,318
[soft music playing]

502
00:31:11,995 --> 00:31:13,705
I mean, as a friend.

503
00:31:19,252 --> 00:31:21,629
Ever since we were kids,
you're all I have.

504
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:25,049
You're my family and my only friend.

505
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:28,970
Remember when you saved me?

506
00:31:30,847 --> 00:31:33,099
You gave my life direction.

507
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:36,185
So, there's nothing
I wouldn't do for you, Ivy.

508
00:31:38,771 --> 00:31:41,649
[soft music playing]

509
00:31:44,110 --> 00:31:45,403
Thank you, Jepoy.

510
00:31:47,155 --> 00:31:48,323
For everything.

511
00:31:52,660 --> 00:31:53,828
Take care of yourself.

512
00:31:55,330 --> 00:31:58,708
[soft music playing]

513
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:19,020
Papa, you're right about Ivy.
She's just playing with us.

514
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:22,023
I don't know if she just convinced Diego,

515
00:32:22,106 --> 00:32:23,358
or they've always been accomplices,

516
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:26,736
but my point is, they can't be trusted.

517
00:32:26,819 --> 00:32:32,408
Emilia, we can't trust anyone anymore.

518
00:32:32,492 --> 00:32:36,829
Not even your closest friends
or most loyal servants.

519
00:32:36,913 --> 00:32:38,706
[sinister music playing]

520
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:42,585
Sometimes, not even your own family.

521
00:32:45,088 --> 00:32:48,299
I guess that's really how it is now.

522
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:50,927
[tense music playing]

523
00:32:52,345 --> 00:32:53,638
You might be allies today…

524
00:32:57,183 --> 00:32:58,601
but enemies tomorrow.

525
00:33:00,019 --> 00:33:01,020
[Julio chuckles]

526
00:33:01,437 --> 00:33:05,692
Good thing I can easily spot
those dirty moles.

527
00:33:09,278 --> 00:33:13,866
[Julio] <i>I can smell traitors</i>
<i>from a mile away.</i>

528
00:33:17,245 --> 00:33:19,163
<i>And I'll always catch them in the act.</i>

529
00:33:19,831 --> 00:33:23,751
[tense music playing]

530
00:33:35,888 --> 00:33:38,391
[action music playing]

531
00:33:44,063 --> 00:33:45,064
[door closes]

532
00:33:46,190 --> 00:33:49,068
[action music playing]

533
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:08,629
[tense music swelling]

534
00:34:39,368 --> 00:34:40,578
Grandpa, Mama…

535
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:43,998
Excuse me. You have to see this.

536
00:34:47,168 --> 00:34:48,920
Spot the hero here.

537
00:34:50,046 --> 00:34:51,506
[suspenseful music]

538
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:55,301
-[scoffs]
-[Emilia] Oh.

539
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:57,011
I knew it.

540
00:34:57,095 --> 00:34:58,304
[Emilia] Madrigal?

541
00:35:00,264 --> 00:35:01,891
Good work, Arnaldo.

542
00:35:02,558 --> 00:35:05,311
We finally caught the rat.

543
00:35:05,394 --> 00:35:06,354
[chuckling]

544
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:10,900
[dramatic music]

545
00:35:16,823 --> 00:35:18,449
[soft music playing]

546
00:35:25,456 --> 00:35:27,083
[Ivy] <i>Where are the other witnesses?</i>

547
00:35:27,875 --> 00:35:29,210
<i>Lily, they're all dead.</i>

548
00:35:29,293 --> 00:35:30,586
[screams]

549
00:35:31,295 --> 00:35:33,589
<i>After everything we've done!</i>

550
00:35:33,923 --> 00:35:37,552
<i>Miss Ivy, I have a favor to ask.</i>
<i>Get my family out of here</i>

551
00:35:37,635 --> 00:35:38,928
<i>so they won't get dragged into all this.</i>

552
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:41,848
[Georgina] <i>Mr. Vidal, did the former</i>

553
00:35:41,931 --> 00:35:45,810
<i>governor order you to rape</i>
<i>and kill Camia Cruz?</i>

554
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:47,520
<i>No, Your Honor.</i>

555
00:35:47,728 --> 00:35:49,605
<i>The Ardientes would've killed my family</i>

556
00:35:49,689 --> 00:35:51,816
<i>if I didn't retract my statement.</i>

557
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:53,901
<i>Due to insufficient testimonies,</i>

558
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:57,446
<i>Emilia Ardiente-Torillo and Raul Torillo…</i>

559
00:35:57,530 --> 00:36:00,449
<i>are hereby declared innocent</i>
<i>of the rape, abduction,</i>

560
00:36:00,533 --> 00:36:03,619
<i>and illegal imprisonment of Camia Cruz.</i>

561
00:36:11,502 --> 00:36:12,503
Mom.

562
00:36:15,923 --> 00:36:16,924
Lily.

563
00:36:18,301 --> 00:36:23,472
More innocents have died
at the hands of the Ardientes.

564
00:36:24,974 --> 00:36:26,934
I can't stop thinking that

565
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:31,898
if it weren't for us,
this wouldn't have happened.

566
00:36:31,981 --> 00:36:33,357
[instrumental theme music playing]

567
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:34,609
Mom…

568
00:36:37,570 --> 00:36:41,991
Don't say that.
We didn't do anything wrong.

569
00:36:43,034 --> 00:36:46,954
What the Ardientes did is not our fault.

570
00:36:48,664 --> 00:36:51,000
If we let them overwhelm us,

571
00:36:52,001 --> 00:36:55,213
no one else will have
the courage to fight them.

572
00:36:56,964 --> 00:36:58,257
Let them gloat.

573
00:36:58,341 --> 00:37:00,301
If they think they've won,

574
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:03,763
they're wrong.

575
00:37:05,973 --> 00:37:07,391
Because I'll never give up.

576
00:37:08,935 --> 00:37:10,478
We'll never give up.

577
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:26,494
[action music playing]

578
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:39,632
[Julio] <i>What do you mean?</i>

579
00:37:40,466 --> 00:37:44,095
<i>Tonio was able to leave</i>
<i>the country without us knowing?</i>

580
00:37:44,178 --> 00:37:46,889
[Arnaldo] <i>Someone helped them.</i>

581
00:37:46,973 --> 00:37:48,891
[Emilia] <i>The question is, who?</i>

582
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:51,102
<i>Camia doesn't have the resources</i>
<i>to do that.</i>

583
00:37:51,185 --> 00:37:54,063
[Arnaldo] <i>I'm suspecting Senator Magno,</i>

584
00:37:54,146 --> 00:37:55,564
<i>but we're not sure yet.</i>

585
00:37:55,648 --> 00:37:59,068
[Emilia] <i>How can we make sure</i>
<i>Tonio will keep quiet?</i>

586
00:37:59,986 --> 00:38:02,738
[Arnaldo] <i>After I threatened</i>
<i>Tonio and his family,</i>

587
00:38:02,822 --> 00:38:04,156
<i>I'm sure he'll keep his mouth shut.</i>

588
00:38:04,949 --> 00:38:07,868
<i>One more slip-up, and I'll wipe them out.</i>

589
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:10,705
<i>Just like I took care of</i>
<i>all the other witnesses.</i>

590
00:38:11,330 --> 00:38:12,081
[Emilia] <i>As for me,</i>

591
00:38:12,164 --> 00:38:15,626
<i>I'll silence Camia once and for all</i>
<i>to solve our problem.</i>

592
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:18,212
[Julio] <i>Slow down, Emilia.</i>

593
00:38:18,296 --> 00:38:21,340
<i>She's too high a risk</i>
<i>to take on right now.</i>

594
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:29,807
[Magno] Oh, thank you.

595
00:38:30,808 --> 00:38:32,893
[tense music playing]

596
00:38:33,269 --> 00:38:38,232
Senator Magno? Senator,
it's so nice to see you here!

597
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:40,359
-Hi, Miss Aguas!
-Hello!

598
00:38:40,443 --> 00:38:43,446
Have you met my wife?
Cecil, this is Ivy Aguas.

599
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:45,990
-Hello!
-Hi, Cecil. Nice to meet you.

600
00:38:47,325 --> 00:38:50,411
Senator, I'm so sorry
I disturbed your date night.

601
00:38:50,494 --> 00:38:51,287
It's okay.

602
00:38:51,370 --> 00:38:53,664
I hope we can arrange a meeting soon?

603
00:38:53,748 --> 00:38:54,999
A meeting? For what?

604
00:38:55,499 --> 00:38:58,836
Aren't you supporting the
Ardientes with their campaign?

605
00:38:59,503 --> 00:39:00,504
[chuckles]

606
00:39:01,797 --> 00:39:06,052
Senator, with the controversies
piling up against the Ardientes,

607
00:39:06,135 --> 00:39:08,346
I don't know if it's the right decision

608
00:39:08,429 --> 00:39:10,598
to keep supporting them.

609
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:15,269
I want to support someone
who has principles…

610
00:39:15,603 --> 00:39:21,108
a firm resolve, and a heart
for the common people.

611
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:25,237
I hope I'm talking
to the right person now.

612
00:39:26,530 --> 00:39:28,741
Okay, I'll tell my secretary to call you.

613
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:32,578
Thank you, Senator. Thank you.

614
00:39:33,412 --> 00:39:35,456
-You're welcome.
-Enjoy. Enjoy your date.

615
00:39:35,748 --> 00:39:38,042
Nice meeting you, Cecil!

616
00:39:38,709 --> 00:39:40,169
Senator, thank you.

617
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:41,879
You're welcome.

618
00:39:44,131 --> 00:39:46,384
[tense music playing]

619
00:39:49,220 --> 00:39:50,304
[phone ringing]

620
00:39:52,765 --> 00:39:53,933
[phone ringing]

621
00:39:54,934 --> 00:39:55,935
[line ringing]

622
00:39:56,143 --> 00:39:57,186
[door opening]

623
00:39:57,269 --> 00:39:58,145
Hands up!

624
00:39:58,229 --> 00:39:59,355
[line ringing]

625
00:40:01,649 --> 00:40:02,775
[line ringing]

626
00:40:04,693 --> 00:40:06,779
-You recorded it.
-[line ringing]

627
00:40:07,696 --> 00:40:09,907
Who's on the phone? Give me that.

628
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:13,035
[Arnaldo grunts]

629
00:40:14,078 --> 00:40:15,079
[line ringing]

630
00:40:16,330 --> 00:40:17,456
[phone ringing]

631
00:40:19,208 --> 00:40:20,084
Hey!

632
00:40:20,167 --> 00:40:21,252
[Jepoy and Arnaldo grunting]

633
00:40:21,335 --> 00:40:22,461
[phone ringing]

634
00:40:24,797 --> 00:40:25,798
Jepoy?

635
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:29,677
[action music playing]

636
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:30,761
Jepoy?

637
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:37,435
[Arnaldo] Give me that! Give it to me!

638
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:41,814
[goon] Take it.

639
00:40:41,897 --> 00:40:43,732
Hold him still. Make him stand.

640
00:40:51,073 --> 00:40:52,783
[action music playing]

641
00:40:53,617 --> 00:40:56,662
Good. Very well-played, Madrigal.

642
00:40:57,663 --> 00:41:00,082
I don't need to scare you, do I?

643
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:03,169
You know what I do to our enemies.

644
00:41:03,252 --> 00:41:05,087
So, spit it out.

645
00:41:06,046 --> 00:41:09,925
Come on. Spit it out! Out with it!

646
00:41:11,260 --> 00:41:12,344
[Jepoy grunts]

647
00:41:12,761 --> 00:41:16,265
-[goon] Stand up!
-Come on. Spit it out.

648
00:41:17,224 --> 00:41:18,309
Spit it out!

649
00:41:22,354 --> 00:41:24,273
[action music playing]

650
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:35,784
[Jepoy coughing]

651
00:41:45,211 --> 00:41:47,046
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

652
00:41:47,129 --> 00:41:48,714
<i>Please try again later.</i>

653
00:41:48,797 --> 00:41:52,009
[action music playing]

654
00:41:55,471 --> 00:41:57,765
[brooding music playing]

655
00:41:57,848 --> 00:41:58,974
He's all yours.

656
00:42:07,274 --> 00:42:10,694
I want you to search his room thoroughly.

657
00:42:11,195 --> 00:42:15,241
I want to know exactly
who this bastard works for.

658
00:42:19,495 --> 00:42:21,163
[brooding music playing]

659
00:42:23,165 --> 00:42:24,792
You're wasting your time.

660
00:42:26,669 --> 00:42:28,128
You'll never get anything from me.

661
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:33,092
[goon] Sir.

662
00:42:33,175 --> 00:42:34,760
Nothing, huh?

663
00:42:37,388 --> 00:42:38,389
Hmm…

664
00:42:39,306 --> 00:42:40,307
Hey.

665
00:42:41,767 --> 00:42:47,856
How are you connected to Magno?
Is he your boss?

666
00:42:48,148 --> 00:42:49,650
[breathing heavily]

667
00:42:49,733 --> 00:42:50,734
Well?!

668
00:42:50,985 --> 00:42:52,278
[Julio chuckles]

669
00:42:52,778 --> 00:42:55,072
He's tough, Grandpa. We
won't get him to spill anything.

670
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:59,702
Arnaldo, I've seen a lot
of tough men in my life.

671
00:43:01,495 --> 00:43:03,747
So let's test how tough he really is.

672
00:43:05,332 --> 00:43:06,709
Take him to the dungeon.

673
00:43:07,835 --> 00:43:08,836
Go!

674
00:43:18,721 --> 00:43:19,805
[line ringing]

675
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:23,100
Ivy, are you okay?

676
00:43:25,185 --> 00:43:26,312
No, I'm not.

677
00:43:26,395 --> 00:43:28,731
Because Jepoy's
still not answering his phone.

678
00:43:29,315 --> 00:43:30,566
He rang my phone last night.

679
00:43:30,649 --> 00:43:32,693
But he didn't pick up
when I tried to call him back.

680
00:43:33,319 --> 00:43:35,029
I'm worried about him, Diego.

681
00:43:35,362 --> 00:43:40,034
Jepoy always gives me updates
on what the Ardientes are up to.

682
00:43:40,367 --> 00:43:41,493
I'll ask my dad.

683
00:43:41,994 --> 00:43:43,746
No! No.

684
00:43:44,580 --> 00:43:45,914
Don't you dare do that.

685
00:43:46,373 --> 00:43:48,584
Didn't I tell you
that I don't trust your father?

686
00:43:49,168 --> 00:43:51,378
What if he puts Jepoy's life in danger?

687
00:43:52,129 --> 00:43:53,881
[tense music playing]

688
00:43:55,758 --> 00:43:58,052
Maybe I should just go
to the Ardientes' mansion?

689
00:43:58,135 --> 00:44:01,805
Don't. Ivy, the Ardientes are
growing suspicious of you now.

690
00:44:02,139 --> 00:44:03,807
What if they're just setting you up?

691
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:07,853
I don't care. I need to save Jepoy.

692
00:44:09,396 --> 00:44:11,482
Is that how important Jepoy is to you?

693
00:44:12,024 --> 00:44:12,816
Yes.

694
00:44:15,611 --> 00:44:16,612
Yes, Diego.

695
00:44:19,156 --> 00:44:21,116
Jepoy's important to me.

696
00:44:21,742 --> 00:44:23,160
He's done so much for me.

697
00:44:23,243 --> 00:44:25,746
He's sacrificed a lot just
so I can carry out my plans.

698
00:44:27,164 --> 00:44:30,417
That's why I need to do
something to save Jepoy.

699
00:44:31,251 --> 00:44:34,380
[melancholic music playing]

700
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:40,552
Don't worry. I'll call you, okay?

701
00:44:55,651 --> 00:44:57,653
Um… I'll just get changed.

702
00:45:03,158 --> 00:45:05,828
<i>-Ouch!</i>
<i>-Be careful. Your wound is deep.</i>

703
00:45:06,912 --> 00:45:10,541
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

704
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:23,137
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

705
00:45:35,816 --> 00:45:36,859
<i>I'm okay now.</i>

706
00:45:38,152 --> 00:45:39,820
<i>No, you should rest first.</i>

707
00:45:42,030 --> 00:45:43,782
<i>No, Diego. I'm fine. Thank you.</i>

708
00:45:44,825 --> 00:45:46,118
Ivy, you need to rest.

709
00:45:48,954 --> 00:45:50,372
I need to get moving.

710
00:45:52,624 --> 00:45:55,752
We both know the Ardientes
are already making

711
00:45:55,836 --> 00:45:57,629
their move as we speak.

712
00:45:58,964 --> 00:46:01,758
We have no idea who they're torturing

713
00:46:01,842 --> 00:46:03,719
or who they'll kill next.

714
00:46:07,055 --> 00:46:08,724
That's why I need to act now.

715
00:46:24,072 --> 00:46:25,949
-Ivy.
-Emilia.

716
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:28,744
What brings you here?

717
00:46:29,745 --> 00:46:30,746
Uh…

718
00:46:30,871 --> 00:46:32,372
Are you still upset with me?

719
00:46:32,873 --> 00:46:35,626
I was worried you got offended
by what I did.

720
00:46:36,126 --> 00:46:39,171
So, I brought you some flowers
as a peace offering.

721
00:46:40,380 --> 00:46:42,424
Thank you. But, it's okay,
don't worry about it.

722
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:47,262
Wait, can I offer you anything?
Juice, coffee, tea, or wine?

723
00:46:48,472 --> 00:46:50,057
-Water would be fine.
-All right.

724
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:51,433
I'll just bring this to the kitchen

725
00:46:51,517 --> 00:46:53,060
and put it in a vase to keep them fresh.

726
00:46:53,143 --> 00:46:53,977
-Okay.
-Hold on.

727
00:46:54,061 --> 00:46:56,188
-I'll just stay here.
-Maid, come with me.

728
00:47:03,195 --> 00:47:04,696
Throw this away.

729
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:07,449
[sinister music playing]

730
00:47:14,373 --> 00:47:19,253
You know what, Madrigal?
I'm mad because I was outwitted.

731
00:47:20,629 --> 00:47:23,590
But do you know what makes me feel worse?

732
00:47:23,674 --> 00:47:27,511
It's the fact that I was
outwitted by a mere bodyguard!

733
00:47:27,594 --> 00:47:29,096
[grunts]

734
00:47:30,180 --> 00:47:36,478
You bastard! I trusted you!
And this is how you repay me?!

735
00:47:37,729 --> 00:47:38,730
Hmm?!

736
00:47:39,815 --> 00:47:42,985
Hey! Don't doze off! Open your eyes!

737
00:47:43,068 --> 00:47:46,947
I'm not done with you!
I'm just getting started!

738
00:47:47,030 --> 00:47:49,449
I'll make you pay, Madrigal.

739
00:47:49,533 --> 00:47:50,951
I'll teach you a lesson,

740
00:47:51,034 --> 00:47:52,786
one you won't forget.

741
00:47:52,869 --> 00:47:55,122
Does it hurt?!

742
00:47:55,205 --> 00:47:56,290
[Jepoy retches]

743
00:47:56,373 --> 00:47:59,126
Go on! Spit it out! Go ahead!

744
00:48:00,586 --> 00:48:01,837
Bastard!

745
00:48:03,463 --> 00:48:04,464
[coughing]

746
00:48:04,548 --> 00:48:06,967
Congressman, Mrs. Emilia's on the phone.

747
00:48:10,095 --> 00:48:11,471
Hello?

748
00:48:11,555 --> 00:48:12,598
Hello, Papa.

749
00:48:12,681 --> 00:48:15,350
Ivy's here. Can I bring her there?

750
00:48:15,851 --> 00:48:17,019
Why? What are you up to?

751
00:48:25,902 --> 00:48:29,239
<i>This is Papa's happy place. Surprise.</i>

752
00:48:29,323 --> 00:48:30,949
[Julio] <i>I just want you to see</i>

753
00:48:31,033 --> 00:48:37,706
<i>what we do to anyone</i>
<i>who betrays the Ardientes!</i>

754
00:48:37,789 --> 00:48:39,958
<i>I need to save Jepoy.</i>

755
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:42,502
<i>I will never forgive myself</i>
<i>if something bad happens to you.</i>

756
00:48:42,586 --> 00:48:46,298
<i>And I won't forgive myself</i>
<i>if I let them kill Jepoy!</i>

757
00:48:47,549 --> 00:48:49,468
<i>You will tell me who your boss is.</i>

758
00:48:49,551 --> 00:48:52,137
<i>If you don't, I'll drill this</i>
<i>into your forehead.</i>

759
00:48:52,804 --> 00:48:55,891
<i>Okay, Grandpa. I'll take care of</i>
<i>Camia Cruz. You can count on me.</i>

760
00:48:55,974 --> 00:48:57,309
<i>Go on. Break into the house.</i>

761
00:48:58,935 --> 00:49:01,855
[theme music playing]
